6. AI/ML applications
==========================

Conduct downscaling model archtecture review and evaluate deep learning pipelines using U-Transformer architecture and residual diffusion for precipitation downscaling. These models utilize 72 variables to improve accuracy compared to existing generative adversarial networks.

Evaluations across 3 flood events reveal that quantile mapping requires seasonal adjustments to avoid overestimation. The CONUS404 dataset should be used as reference data rather than ground truth to ensure scientific accuracy.

There is computational trade-off required for high-accuracy diffusion models against faster baseline methods. Strategic alignment focuses on generating robust statistical samples for extreme precipitation events rather than seeking universal model perfection.

